  "proof": {
    "algorithm_mutual_exclusion": "A Job cannot execute SLH, XMSS and LMS concurrently. In SLH Sign, FORS macros complete before WOTS macro endpoint writes; there is no in-flight WOTS chain while FORS scratch lives.",
    "root_scratch_nonoverlap": "FORS macro group loop is exactly 0..k-1 for all six validated profiles; k <=35, so roots occupy 0..34 and scratch 36..59 never overlaps.",
    "stack_auth_simultaneous_liveness": "Tree-stack and auth-path data survive FORS microgroups; their 68..107 addresses remain disjoint from scratch, so no algorithm-mutual-exclusion shortcut covers live same-operation data.",
    "scratch_lifetime": "Scratch first receives FORS leaves, then level-1 parents and level-2 roots, in place. FORS_ROOT_NEXT consumes group roots in sequence into the existing stack. All roots are consumed before CHAIN_SETUP starts the next microgroup. Final macro root is stored at group_index <=34.",
    "scalar_path": "P1 never asserts fors_leaves/fors_pipe; FORS uses scalar hash and existing node/stack/auth. Shrink affects memory mapping only.",
    "capacity": "67 endpoints, 35 FORS roots, 20 stack, 20 auth and 24 scratch all retained. Scratch aliases endpoint 36..59 only while those endpoints are dead.",
    "parity": "New base36 is even, same as old112; all adjacency and in-place pair parity preserved.",
    "tail_reads": "AUTH_OUTPUT speculates one beyond last valid node: read0=108/read1=109, both remain <128. List guard remains67; pipeline scratch guard60 remains available. Clamp127/126 preserves opposite-bank rule at final physical slot."
  },
